<title>USA: Minn. House committee rejects Twins stadium bill.</title>
<headline>Minn. House committee rejects Twins stadium bill.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>- A Minnesota House Committee voted 10 to 9 Wednesday night not to advance a bill to help finance a new stadium for the Minnesota Twins baseball team, the Star Tribune reported Thursday.</p>
<p>But bill supporters said the measure was not dead this session despite the rejection by the House Local Government and Metropolitan Affairs Committee, the paper said.</p>
<p>Last week, the Senate Committee on Local and Metropolitan Government eliminated public funding for the stadium from a similar bill before approving it.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
